    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where $ t' = t_{\\mathrm{FS}} - t_{\\mathrm{PHS}} $, and $ \\phi = 1 - t_{\\mathrm{FS}} + nt' $. The standard error of $ h^2 = 4t_{\\mathrm{PHS}} $ is $ 4\\sqrt{\\mathrm{Var}(t_{\\mathrm{PHS}})} $.",
      "source_page": 590,
      "printed_page": 570,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter18:p024:b14"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        152.0,
